            },
            {
              "_key": "k50",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k51",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Employer B's Part B shows ₹6,00,000 in row 1(e), salary from the previous employer, because Ishita submitted Form 12B. Employer B worked out tax on the combined ₹16,50,000 under the new regime, subtracted Employer A's ₹18,000, and spread the balance over seven months. Together the two employers deducted ₹1,20,900, exactly the tax on her salary alone.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "warning",
              "text": "Ishita notes that her salary for the return is ₹6,00,000 plus ₹10,50,000, entered once each. The ₹6,00,000 in Employer B's row 1(e) is not a third salary.",
              "_key": "k52"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k53",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k54",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Step 2: Form 26AS Reveals a Gap",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k55",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k56",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "On 16 June she downloads Form 26AS for AY 2026-27. Employer B shows ₹1,02,900, HDFC Bank ₹7,200 and Infosys ₹1,200, all with status F. Employer A shows only ₹10,800.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k57",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k58",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "The missing ₹7,200 is exactly July and August, Employer A's Q2. Her Part A shows it was deducted and gives a receipt number for Q2, so the statement was filed. The likeliest cause is a problem with her entry in that statement. On 18 June she emails Employer A's payroll team with her PAN, the TAN, the quarter, the amount, her Part A and her July and August payslips, asking for a correction statement.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k59",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k60",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Step 3: AIS Reveals Two Wrong Entries",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k61",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k62",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Next she downloads AIS as CSV for FY 2025-26 and goes through it line by line.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
