              "_key": "k138"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k139",
              "_type": "collapsible",
              "title": "Show me the full working",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_key": "k140",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k141",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "HRA exemption, month by month.",
                      "marks": [
                        "strong"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "_key": "k142",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": " At Employer A, basic salary was ₹48,000 a month and HRA ₹24,000. Rent of ₹30,000 minus 10% of basic is ₹25,200, and 40% of basic is ₹19,200, so ₹19,200 a month is exempt for 5 months: ₹96,000. At Employer B, basic was ₹60,000 and HRA ₹30,000. Rent minus 10% of basic is ₹24,000, and 40% of basic is ₹24,000, so ₹24,000 a month for 7 months: ₹1,68,000. Total ₹2,64,000. Hyderabad gets the 40% limit for FY 2025-26.",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k143",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k144",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Old regime slab income.",
                      "marks": [
                        "strong"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "_key": "k145",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": " ₹16,50,000 minus ₹2,64,000 HRA, ₹50,000 standard deduction and ₹2,400 professional tax = ₹13,33,600 salary. Add ₹78,800 interest and ₹15,500 dividends = ₹14,27,900. Deduct 80C ₹1,50,000 (EPF), 80D ₹25,000 and ₹6,800 savings interest = ₹12,46,100. Slab tax: ₹12,500 + ₹1,00,000 + 30% of ₹2,46,100 (₹73,830) = ₹1,86,330.",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k146",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k147",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "New regime slab income.",
                      "marks": [
                        "strong"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "_key": "k148",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": " ₹16,50,000 minus ₹75,000 = ₹15,75,000 salary. Add ₹78,800 interest and ₹15,500 dividends = ₹16,69,300. Slab tax: ₹20,000 + ₹40,000 + ₹60,000 + 20% of ₹69,300 (₹13,860) = ₹1,33,860.",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k149",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k150",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Capital gains.",
                      "marks": [
                        "strong"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "_key": "k151",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": " Shares: ₹3,90,000 minus ₹3,50,000 = ₹40,000 short term, at 20% = ₹8,000. Fund: ₹6,00,000 minus ₹4,40,000 = ₹1,60,000 long term. The first ₹1,25,000 is exempt, so ₹35,000 at 12.5% = ₹4,375.",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k152",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k153",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Cess and total.",
                      "marks": [
                        "strong"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "_key": "k154",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": " Old: ₹1,98,705 plus cess ₹7,948.20 = ₹2,06,653.20, rounded to ₹2,06,650. New: ₹1,46,235 plus cess ₹5,849.40 = ₹1,52,084.40, rounded to ₹1,52,080.",
                      "marks": []
